header and decides what an unattested request may do. The framework never blocks or fails your requests: when no token is available, the request is sent without the header."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It builds on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPinKit"},{"text":": set up certificate pinning first, because every call to your verifier is pinned by the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPin"},{"text":" instance with the same identifier, and register the verifier’s domain in your TrustPin project. Tokens can be bound to the user’s session so that a token cannot be replayed outside it. For an operation your backend must not accept on a reused token alone, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPinAttest\/assertionHeaders(payloadDigest:)"},{"text":" adds an assertion bound to that operation. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reports what the framework did, for your metrics.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"TrustPinAttestKit 7.1.0 requires an attestation verifier at contract version 2 or later. Use the framework from the app process: app extensions are not supported.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Getting-started","type":"heading","text":"Getting started"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AttestVerifierURL"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AttestedHosts"},{"type":"text","text":" to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPin-Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":" that holds your pinning configuration, then:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import TrustPinKit","import TrustPinAttestKit","","try await TrustPin.setup(.fromPlist())","try await TrustPinAttest.setup(.fromPlist())","","TrustPinAttest.bindToHeader(\"Authorization\")   \/\/